{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3FWSUhLuCBzhz2t4fdx","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I haven't changed anything for this one, because a per-day breakdown in `out/summary.csv` would break the file for the partner.\n\n**The conflict:** the README says `out/summary.csv` must stay under 50 lines and that the partner portal silently truncates anything longer. Today the file has 12 lines: a header plus 11 monthly rows. A per-day breakdown for 2025 needs up to 365 rows. The portal would keep only the first 49 or so, roughly January and part of February, and give no error. The partner would just see an incomplete year. Adding the daily rows alongside the monthly ones has the same problem.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **A separate file**, e.g. `out/summary_daily.csv` with the same `period,total,count` columns and one row per day. `summary.csv` stays as it is. This is what I'd recommend, but it only helps if the partner can pull a second file from the portal, which I can't check from here.\n2. **One file per month**, e.g. `out/daily/2025-01.csv`, each with at most 31 rows. Use this if the portal applies the 50-line limit to every file it pulls.\n3. **Keep it inside `summary.csv` with a coarser breakdown**, such as weekly totals. That's 53 rows for 2025, which is still over the limit, so it only works if you narrow the date range.\n\nWhich of these does the partner's portal support? Once you tell me, I'll make the change in `scripts/summarize.py` or a sibling script, run it, and commit.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":512,"cache_read_input_tokens":19428,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":512,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":